# Root-level .dockerignore — applies to every service whose docker-compose
# build context is the repo root: intake-service and eligibility-service
# (adr/0005-eligibility-agent-runtime-and-resilience.md), records-service
# (Stage 3 — imports libs.patient_view_agent), gateway (it must copy
# config/roles.yaml, the live RBAC permission source, which lives outside its
# own directory), and now scheduling-service, interop-service, and
# roi-service (OBS-M02, Stage 7 smoke-test discovery: all three import
# libs/ — libs.safe_logging, and scheduling/roi's Stage 6 libs.metrics —
# which a per-service build context could never see; the image built fine
# but the container crashed at startup with ModuleNotFoundError, invisible
# to CI and to pytest, which imports directly from the repo checkout).
#
# Every root-context service now needs every other service's directory
# present in the context (none is excluded below) — that costs a few KB of
# context and nothing else, since each Dockerfile only COPYs the paths it
# names.
.git/
.github/
frontend/
node_modules/
docs/
adr/
tests/
.claude/
.codex_tmp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# db/ is mounted into the Postgres container at runtime (docker-compose.yml);
# it is not part of any Python service's build.
#
# w8-planner-2 P2 (adr/0012), review round 1 fix (B1): TWO exceptions —
# intake-service's Dockerfile COPYs the ssn/dob/notes backfill script
# (db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_existing_phi.py), and records-service's
# Dockerfile COPYs the agent-draft-text backfill script (adr/0012
# follow-up, db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_agent_draft_text.py) — so
# `make up`/`make seed`/`make phi-backfill` can run both via `docker
# compose exec`. The negation is listed at every parent level for each; a
# bare `!db/migrations/scripts/<file>` alone does not re-include a file
# whose ancestor directory was already excluded.
db/
!db/migrations/
!db/migrations/scripts/
!db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_existing_phi.py
!db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_agent_draft_text.py
